1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,550
[wind blowing]

2
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:07,390
[SITARA] What?

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:10,980
Princess Sorghaghtani
refused the marriage after all?

4
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:12,730
That's right.
Quite surprising, isn't it?

5
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:14,140
So what will happen
to Lady Töregene?

6
00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:15,310
Her freedom depended

7
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:17,230
on the princess marrying
Prince Güyük!

8
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:19,360
What did Empress Boraqchin
have to say about it?

9
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:22,360
Calm down, will you?
I'll tell you everything.

10
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:27,490
Sorghaghtani Beki.

11
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:29,950
This is what is best
for the Mongols.

12
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:32,370
And it is to your benefit
as well.

13
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:36,880
I must recommend that you humbly
accept our offer.

14
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,210
♪

15
00:00:38,630 --> 00:00:41,210
I truly appreciate
your courtesy.

16
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:44,510
However, I then remember
the wise words

17
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:45,970
our great foremother,

18
00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:47,800
Alan Gua, said to her five sons:

19
00:00:47,890 --> 00:00:50,520
"A single arrow may be broken
with ease

20
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,600
but five arrows bundled together
shan't ever be broken."

21
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:55,850
Great Kha'an,

22
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:59,150
Tolui was one of the arrows
bundled at your side.

23
00:00:59,230 --> 00:01:01,940
It falls upon me
to raise his sons.

24
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:03,860
They are young
and fragile arrows

25
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:05,780
still needing to be crafted.

26
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:09,370
[BORAQCHIN]
The House of Tolui on its own?

27
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:13,160
She refuses to be engulfed
by the House of Ögedei.

28
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:15,540
[SORGHAGHTANI]
I'm quite sure your retainers

29
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:17,170
-feel the same way.
-[gasps]

30
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:19,000
Isn't that right, General Ilüge?

31
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,500
Huh? Uh, yes.

32
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:22,250
[SORGHAGHTANI]
You are the head retainer

33
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:23,420
serving the House of Ögedei.

34
00:01:23,510 --> 00:01:25,130
I imagine the Great Kha'an

35
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:26,880
trusts you
with his finest treasure.

36
00:01:26,970 --> 00:01:29,850
A sign of his
utmost confidence in you.

37
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:33,140
[SITARA] His finest treasure?

38
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:35,310
Does she mean Lady Töregene?

39
00:01:35,390 --> 00:01:36,560
Yes.

40
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:38,690
She's in
General Ilüge's territory.

41
00:01:38,770 --> 00:01:39,940
[Ilüge groans]

42
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:43,940
[♪ opening theme song playing]

43
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:15,280
[ÖGEDEI]
You seem to be in a foul mood.

44
00:03:17,450 --> 00:03:18,580
[BORAQCHIN] Do I?

45
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:21,460
Sorghaghtani sent a messenger.

46
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:24,130
If it's to the
Great Kha'an's liking,

47
00:03:24,210 --> 00:03:26,800
she's happy
to offer up 4,000 tents

48
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:28,670
from the House of Tolui.

49
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,880
The same territory and people

50
00:03:30,970 --> 00:03:34,010
I had planned to deprive her of
all along.

51
00:03:34,850 --> 00:03:36,930
She's making a mockery of me.

52
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:39,980
Are you angry at me

53
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:41,890
for what I have done
to your family?

54
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,310
[ÖGEDEI] How could I be angry?

55
00:03:44,730 --> 00:03:48,440
Because of you, I am finally
able to do as I wish.

56
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:50,280
You have my thanks.

57
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:54,280
However, I must say this,

58
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:56,120
going forward,

59
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:58,450
please don't involve
Töregene anymore.

60
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,040
She is someone precious to me.
I want her protected.

61
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:06,290
I understand.

62
00:04:07,710 --> 00:04:09,300
[SHIRA]
Prince Güyük and Sir Qadaq

63
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:11,550
are heading
for General Ilüge's lands.

64
00:04:11,630 --> 00:04:14,130
General Ilüge served
as the Great Kha'an's tutor

65
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,300
for many years.

66
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:18,470
His influence rivals
that of the imperial family.

67
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,560
Not even Prince Güyük
can just go there

68
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,980
without establishing
a good reason first.

69
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:25,150
Shira, we need to hurry.

70
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,310
You'd better hold on tight then.

71
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,770
Let's go.

72
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,530
[SHIRA] Looks like
a rough road ahead of us.

73
00:04:32,610 --> 00:04:33,610
♪

74
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,120
[SLAVE] Uh? [exclaims]

75
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:46,130
Excuse me, Lady Töregene.

76
00:04:46,210 --> 00:04:47,500
-[slave exclaims]
-[WOMAN] Uh?

77
00:04:48,210 --> 00:04:49,250
[chuckles]

78
00:04:49,550 --> 00:04:51,960
Have you mistaken me
for that silly girl again?

79
00:04:52,050 --> 00:04:54,130
[slave screams] My apologies.

80
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:57,890
Oh, there are way too many tents

81
00:04:57,970 --> 00:04:59,810
for me to remember
which is which.

82
00:04:59,890 --> 00:05:01,180
-[footsteps]
-Huh?

83
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:03,140
[Qadaq sighs]

84
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:05,190
[ILÜGE] Why,
if it isn't Prince Güyük.

85
00:05:05,270 --> 00:05:07,690
What brings you
to my humble abode?

86
00:05:07,770 --> 00:05:08,770
[GÜYÜK] Uh...

87
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:12,280
Our Lady Töregene is here,
isn't she?

88
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,780
May we speak with her?

89
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:16,320
Now why would you assume
something like that?

90
00:05:17,410 --> 00:05:19,990
Be reasonable.
Would we have come all this way

91
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,790
if we weren't certain?

92
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:25,290
It is kind of a long story,
but let me tell you...

93
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:32,420
[SHIRA] They want us to find her

94
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:33,960
and make sure
that she's still safe

95
00:05:34,050 --> 00:05:36,260
while they try to keep
his attention elsewhere.

96
00:05:36,630 --> 00:05:38,130
Where would we start, even?

97
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:39,430
Forget about success.

98
00:05:39,510 --> 00:05:41,390
If we're caught,
it could mean our heads.

99
00:05:41,470 --> 00:05:42,720
Hey, where are you going?

100
00:05:43,810 --> 00:05:46,350
-[gasps]
-[SHIRA] Hurry.

101
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:49,480
[ELJIGIDEI]
This could be dangerous.

102
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:51,400
We must do everything we can

103
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:53,730
to conceal the fact that
Lady Töregene is here.

104
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:54,940
[Sitara gasps]

105
00:05:55,030 --> 00:05:56,150
[ARGHUN] Hm?

106
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:57,780
Uh?

107
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:00,490
[dog whines]

108
00:06:00,570 --> 00:06:02,910
[ELJIGIDEI]
What's wrong? Let's go.

109
00:06:02,990 --> 00:06:04,080
[ARGHUN] Right.

110
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:06,540
[ELJIGIDEI]
And how is Lady Töregene faring?

111
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:08,580
[ARGHUN]
I went to see her just earlier.

112
00:06:08,670 --> 00:06:09,880
She's doing well.

113
00:06:11,290 --> 00:06:13,750
[sighs] Did you hear
what they said?

114
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:15,840
That means we've confirmed
that she's safe,

115
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,630
and we can head back for now--
[grunts]

116
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,380
Hey, wait! Ah!

117
00:06:24,310 --> 00:06:25,730
[cloth rustles]

118
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:27,440
[footsteps]

119
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:29,770
Lady Töregene,
I thank you for waiting.

120
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:31,060
I've brought your meal.

121
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,520
[sighs] You're late.

122
00:06:33,610 --> 00:06:35,740
[SLAVE] My deepest apologies.

123
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:37,360
I got lost again.

124
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,450
[Töregene sighs]

125
00:06:43,490 --> 00:06:44,870
Why is there no urum?

126
00:06:44,950 --> 00:06:47,160
Hm? Urum's been out of season

127
00:06:47,250 --> 00:06:49,040
for quite some time now,
my lady.

128
00:06:49,370 --> 00:06:52,130
I was just asking.
Now, leave me.

129
00:06:52,210 --> 00:06:53,710
Uh! Of course!

130
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:05,470
[exclaims]

131
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:09,100
Oh, Fatima.

132
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:11,480
[SITARA] Lady Töregene.

133
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:13,730
Lady Töregene.

134
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:16,610
-Lady Töregene.
-[SHIRA] Hey, stop!

135
00:07:16,690 --> 00:07:18,320
-We need to head back!
-[gasps]

136
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:22,200
[SLAVE] Lady Töregene
is so hard to please.

137
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:23,620
[Sitara gasps]

138
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:25,080
♪

139
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:41,550
[gasps softly]

140
00:07:43,010 --> 00:07:44,100
[TÖREGENE] Hm?

141
00:07:44,430 --> 00:07:46,470
[exclaims] Lady Töregene!

142
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:50,140
Fatima? What are you doing here?

143
00:07:50,230 --> 00:07:52,560
Thank goodness.
You're really all right!

144
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,480
I finally get to see you again.

145
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:55,560
[Töregene gasps softly]

146
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:57,150
♪

147
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:00,110
I don't understand.

148
00:08:00,190 --> 00:08:02,200
Even though I betrayed you...

149
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:07,620
[SITARA] Lady Töregene, look.

150
00:08:08,450 --> 00:08:11,660
Despite everything,
you managed to protect them.

151
00:08:12,210 --> 00:08:13,750
All the feelings...

152
00:08:14,670 --> 00:08:17,040
that are the most precious
to me.

153
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:19,090
No.

154
00:08:20,050 --> 00:08:22,010
The most precious to us.

155
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:29,010
[TÖREGENE]
The Great Khatun told me this:

156
00:08:30,350 --> 00:08:34,190
In my previous days,
I waited upon Empress Khulan.

157
00:08:34,730 --> 00:08:36,610
[Töregene gasps] Khulan?

158
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:40,110
The one who taught me
how to find the joys in life.

159
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:42,570
And who offered herself
to the Mongols

160
00:08:42,650 --> 00:08:45,030
to protect the Merkits
facing ruin.

161
00:08:45,110 --> 00:08:46,280
Khulan.

162
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:49,160
[BORAQCHIN] I always had a sense

163
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,700
that she bore
feelings of resentment.

164
00:08:51,790 --> 00:08:53,830
It seems that even to this day,

165
00:08:53,910 --> 00:08:56,380
you harbor those same feelings
toward the Mongols.

166
00:08:56,460 --> 00:08:58,170
Did she really?

167
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:02,920
Please allow me
to lend you my assistance.

168
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:06,680
So that you may be
able to achieve

169
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:08,140
what she wished she could.

170
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:12,520
[TÖREGENE] I thought my chance
to kill Ögedei had come.

171
00:09:13,060 --> 00:09:17,150
The Great Khatun told me
that you were not to be trusted.

172
00:09:17,230 --> 00:09:18,690
[Sitara gasps]

173
00:09:18,770 --> 00:09:20,190
I was a fool.

174
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:24,030
[exclaims] I fell for her lies,

175
00:09:24,110 --> 00:09:26,780
and betrayed
both you and Khulan.

176
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,530
♪

177
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:32,290
[SITARA] Lady Töregene...

178
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:36,290
I, too, found myself confronted.

179
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:40,170
With the thought
of abandoning the past

180
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:42,000
and moving on with my life...

181
00:09:44,470 --> 00:09:47,300
I ended up betraying
you as well.

182
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:51,970
Fatima sure
is taking her time talking.

183
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:54,640
We need to get going
before we're discovered.

184
00:09:54,930 --> 00:09:56,310
[gasps]

185
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:58,520
Wait, is that really
who I think it is?

186
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,650
Uh, no way.

187
00:09:59,730 --> 00:10:01,730
Sorry, but you're
on your own now.

188
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:03,270
[running footsteps]

189
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:05,030
[footsteps]

190
00:10:08,950 --> 00:10:10,700
-[cloth rustles]
-[ÖGEDEI] I'm coming in.

191
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:11,740
[BOTH] Uh?

192
00:10:11,830 --> 00:10:13,120
[gasps]

193
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,370
[SITARA] Great Kha'an!

194
00:10:18,670 --> 00:10:20,460
And what is it you want?

195
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:23,960
If my fate is to be executed,
then let us be done with it.

196
00:10:24,050 --> 00:10:27,130
Of course not.
I have a favor to ask of you.

197
00:10:27,220 --> 00:10:28,300
[TÖREGENE] Hm?

198
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:30,130
You may enter.

199
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,220
-[Töregene gasps]
-Hello, Mother.

200
00:10:34,890 --> 00:10:36,270
My darling Güyük!

201
00:10:36,350 --> 00:10:37,350
[SITARA] "My darling Güyük?"

202
00:10:37,430 --> 00:10:39,440
Oh, my goodness,
what are you doing here,

203
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,560
my little darling?

204
00:10:40,650 --> 00:10:42,150
Is my little boy all right?

205
00:10:42,230 --> 00:10:44,110
You didn't run
into anything scary, did you?

206
00:10:44,190 --> 00:10:46,440
I'm quite well, Mother.
Please try to calm yourself.

207
00:10:46,530 --> 00:10:47,530
[Töregene sighs]

208
00:10:48,610 --> 00:10:52,580
I beg of you, Mother, come back
with me to my territory.

209
00:10:53,530 --> 00:10:54,490
[TÖREGENE] Huh?

210
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:56,080
It lies to the west,

211
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:59,000
on the steppe between the
Altai Mountains and Tian Shan.

212
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:02,960
The winters are cold,
but there's plenty of water.

213
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:05,000
And the pastures are lush.

214
00:11:05,090 --> 00:11:06,630
And what's more,

215
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:08,920
it is far away from here.

216
00:11:09,010 --> 00:11:10,130
[Töregene gasps]

217
00:11:10,630 --> 00:11:11,630
[Sitara gasps softly]

218
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:13,050
♪

219
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:15,850
I ask the same, Töregene.

220
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:20,520
The court is much too tumultuous
a place for you and Güyük, no?

221
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:25,320
If you will agree to go,
I won't ask any more of you.

222
00:11:27,530 --> 00:11:30,320
All I want
is for you to be happy.

223
00:11:33,030 --> 00:11:34,330
[SITARA] I see.

224
00:11:34,410 --> 00:11:36,740
That would certainly resolve
everything tidily.

225
00:11:37,950 --> 00:11:40,080
Empress Boraqchin wanted
Prince Güyük

226
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:42,500
and Princess Sorghaghtani
to get married

227
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:45,250
as a condition
for Lady Töregene's freedom.

228
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:47,750
Her aim was to remove
the three of them

229
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:49,510
from the imperial court.

230
00:11:50,670 --> 00:11:53,640
That particular scheme of hers
didn't bear fruit, though.

231
00:11:54,850 --> 00:11:56,970
But with this plan,
all three of them

232
00:11:57,060 --> 00:11:59,680
will leave the political stage
still the same.

233
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:04,270
And it isn't a terrible proposal
for Lady Töregene, either.

234
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,660
[GÜYÜK] All right then, Mother.

235
00:12:14,490 --> 00:12:17,410
Tomorrow, I'll come fetch you.

236
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:21,830
Sorry for such a commotion.

237
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:23,500
[ILÜGE] Will that be all?

238
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:24,630
[ÖGEDEI] Yes.

239
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:27,920
-But before I go...
-[ILÜGE] Oh?

240
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,380
[ÖGEDEI] Töregene...

241
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:33,930
If I may, can I speak
with your lady-in-waiting?

242
00:12:34,010 --> 00:12:35,010
[TÖREGENE] Huh?

243
00:12:35,090 --> 00:12:36,100
[SITARA] Huh?

244
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:37,350
Oh.

245
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,850
Why do you wanna talk to me?

246
00:12:41,930 --> 00:12:43,940
So you're Fatima, correct?

247
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:46,940
Möge spoke of you.
I hear you get lost easily.

248
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:49,360
Uh...
[chuckles nervously]

249
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:52,780
And I've also heard that
you're a scholar's daughter.

250
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:54,530
Are you knowledgeable
in the stars?

251
00:12:54,610 --> 00:12:55,950
The stars?

252
00:12:56,030 --> 00:12:57,530
[ILÜGE] Please, Great Kha'an!

253
00:12:57,620 --> 00:12:59,280
You really
mustn't speak directly

254
00:12:59,370 --> 00:13:01,250
to someone so far beneath you!

255
00:13:01,330 --> 00:13:02,410
[ÖGEDEI] Hmm.

256
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,790
Allow my son
to relay the words for you.

257
00:13:04,870 --> 00:13:06,330
-Go!
-Oh, all right.

258
00:13:07,790 --> 00:13:09,340
[ELJIGIDEI] The emperor asks,

259
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:11,000
"Are you knowledgeable
in the stars?"

260
00:13:11,090 --> 00:13:14,170
Why, yes. I am. Considerably so.

261
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:18,680
"Why, yes, I am.
Considerably so." Sire!

262
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:20,970
Good. Would she happen to know

263
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:23,140
why the stars move across
the night sky?

264
00:13:23,230 --> 00:13:24,230
[ELJIGIDEI] Oh.

265
00:13:25,060 --> 00:13:26,600
[ELJIGIDEI] "Good.
Would she happen to know

266
00:13:26,690 --> 00:13:28,360
why the stars move
across the night sky?"

267
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:30,020
The Great Kha'an asks.

268
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:31,480
Um...

269
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:33,860
Well, that much I do know.

270
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:36,400
I read it in a book
by Al-Biruni.

271
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:39,950
♪

272
00:13:40,030 --> 00:13:42,580
"He created the sun, moon,
and the stars.

273
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:44,790
All are subject to His command."

274
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:47,040
So it is written in the Quran.

275
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:49,590
This means that
the movement of the stars

276
00:13:49,670 --> 00:13:52,050
is a blessing
granted to us by Allah.

277
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:56,550
Furthermore, the heavens
are eight layers of spheres

278
00:13:56,630 --> 00:13:58,090
revolving in place.

279
00:13:58,180 --> 00:14:01,050
And we reside in the center
of those spheres.

280
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:05,180
-Hmm.
-[ELJIGIDEI] That's a lot.

281
00:14:05,270 --> 00:14:07,230
[ÖGEDEI] Oh? How amusing.

282
00:14:07,310 --> 00:14:09,810
-[Eljigidei gasps]
-Did you say amusing?

283
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:11,360
Hey, you don't talk to him!

284
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:14,280
Yes. Quite different
from what I know.

285
00:14:14,610 --> 00:14:17,990
When I was younger, I was told
that in the night sky,

286
00:14:18,070 --> 00:14:21,200
the stars are livestock
tied to a pillar in heaven.

287
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:23,530
That pillar is the star
in the north sky

288
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:25,000
that never moves.

289
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:26,910
With all due respect,

290
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
-that is merely a superstition.
-[gasps]

291
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,170
[ÖGEDEI] You think so?

292
00:14:30,790 --> 00:14:33,130
For all that we know
and don't know,

293
00:14:33,210 --> 00:14:35,340
our world could be
a galloping horse

294
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:36,550
bound to a rope.

295
00:14:36,630 --> 00:14:38,340
Riding that horse...

296
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:39,970
myself and Boraqchin.

297
00:14:40,050 --> 00:14:41,800
Sorghaghtani and Tolui.

298
00:14:41,890 --> 00:14:43,600
And of course, you and Töregene.

299
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:45,260
All of us on its back,

300
00:14:45,350 --> 00:14:48,430
circling as we head toward
the same destination.

301
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,640
Utter nonsense.

302
00:14:49,730 --> 00:14:51,860
It's against the very concept
of science.

303
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:54,900
-Science, you say?
-[Eljigidei gasps]

304
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:55,900
[Sitara sighs]

305
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:59,450
Yes, science.
The laws that govern nature.

306
00:15:00,070 --> 00:15:01,370
The work of Allah,

307
00:15:01,450 --> 00:15:03,870
who created the world
and bestowed it to us.

308
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:07,160
Science is the discipline
that seeks to study this.

309
00:15:08,790 --> 00:15:10,500
Well, in that case,

310
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:12,750
there are spirits
that the kams speak of.

311
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:15,880
I'd say their existence explains
the laws of nature well enough.

312
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:17,170
You're wrong.

313
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:19,470
The Quran tells us
that Allah made the stars

314
00:15:19,550 --> 00:15:22,390
move across the sky
to help give us direction.

315
00:15:22,470 --> 00:15:24,890
The positions and paths
of the stars are calculated

316
00:15:24,970 --> 00:15:26,180
with Earth at its center,

317
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:28,930
giving us results
without any contradiction.

318
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:30,390
What more proof
could you possibly need

319
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:31,940
to see that this is the truth?

320
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:34,310
Anything else is a mere figment!

321
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:36,190
[breathes heavily]

322
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,320
[wind blows]

323
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:42,240
[Ögedei chuckles]

324
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,410
I see now.

325
00:15:43,910 --> 00:15:46,950
You must get along
very well with Töregene.

326
00:15:47,370 --> 00:15:49,830
What if you and I made a wager?

327
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:52,080
A wager?

328
00:15:52,170 --> 00:15:55,500
[ÖGEDEI] Yes. But one where
all you have to do is watch.

329
00:15:57,340 --> 00:15:58,710
In the days ahead,

330
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:01,420
I will bring prosperity
to the Mongol Empire.

331
00:16:01,510 --> 00:16:04,890
With methods unlike those
of my father or Tolui.

332
00:16:06,010 --> 00:16:09,310
So that you and Töregene
can find happiness.

333
00:16:09,390 --> 00:16:11,020
Find happiness?

334
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:12,940
[ÖGEDEI] That's right.

335
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:15,730
When I first
laid eyes upon Töregene,

336
00:16:15,810 --> 00:16:17,980
I realized what my duty is.

337
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:21,820
I must create
the Mongol Empire anew...

338
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:25,820
Solely because of the look
in her eyes.

339
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:29,910
You've lost your homeland
and family as well, no?

340
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,410
Your eyes earlier,

341
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:35,420
they were the very image
of hers on that day.

342
00:16:38,460 --> 00:16:41,880
So watch me with those
very same eyes of yours.

343
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:45,640
If you two manage
to find happiness here,

344
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:48,260
victory is mine.

345
00:16:48,350 --> 00:16:49,510
♪

346
00:17:19,170 --> 00:17:21,380
[breathing heavily]

347
00:17:23,590 --> 00:17:25,840
[grunting]

348
00:17:25,930 --> 00:17:29,140
[screaming]

349
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:30,680
[thuds]

350
00:17:31,970 --> 00:17:33,770
[panting]

351
00:17:33,850 --> 00:17:35,730
[wind blowing]

352
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:45,530
[bleating]

353
00:18:01,210 --> 00:18:02,130
[TÖREGENE] Fatima?

354
00:18:02,210 --> 00:18:03,590
[Sitara gasps]

355
00:18:03,670 --> 00:18:06,470
-Fatima.
-Oh, Lady Töregene!

356
00:18:06,550 --> 00:18:08,260
Are you all right?

357
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:12,060
Uh, yes. But how are you doing?

358
00:18:13,850 --> 00:18:15,810
You know, Fatima...

359
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,690
I've been thinking
more about it.

360
00:18:26,780 --> 00:18:30,120
I think I won't be going
to live with my Güyük.

361
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,330
[Sitara gasps]

362
00:18:31,410 --> 00:18:33,580
Why, doing that would be

363
00:18:33,660 --> 00:18:35,950
just what
the Great Kha'an wants.

364
00:18:36,450 --> 00:18:39,120
And the very thought of it
infuriates me.

365
00:18:39,210 --> 00:18:40,750
[Sitara gasps]

366
00:18:41,630 --> 00:18:44,500
Fatima, will you...

367
00:18:46,010 --> 00:18:48,920
Will you fight by my side
once more?

368
00:18:49,010 --> 00:18:49,970
♪

369
00:18:50,050 --> 00:18:51,300
[Sitara breathes softly]

370
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,060
The thing is...

371
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:59,100
I'm not clever,
not even a little bit, you know?

372
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:01,060
♪

373
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:11,450
[Sitara gasps]

374
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:16,700
Let the two of us
summon a storm upon them.

375
00:19:17,750 --> 00:19:18,910
[SITARA] That's right.

376
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:22,210
I'm not fighting
the Great Kha'an by myself.

377
00:19:22,290 --> 00:19:24,130
I'm not alone anymore.

378
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:26,880
This empire...

379
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:30,840
And the Mongols who chose to
take everything we had from us.

380
00:19:31,510 --> 00:19:34,390
We can never allow them
to be thought of as good.

381
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:39,100
Fatima, now it's our turn.

382
00:19:43,110 --> 00:19:44,900
To become the witches.

383
00:19:46,730 --> 00:19:49,570
[♪ closing theme song playing]

384
00:21:16,910 --> 00:21:18,620
[wind howling]

385
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:23,000
[SITARA (ADULT)] That year,
the winter came

386
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:25,040
as it always does.

387
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:28,840
And eventually,
so, too, did the summer.

388
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:33,380
On the steppe, the grass sprouts
anew once more,

389
00:21:34,050 --> 00:21:37,640
and the sheep graze peacefully
upon the soft buds.

390
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:38,720
♪

391
00:22:02,830 --> 00:22:05,960
Everything perfectly unchanging.

392
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:10,040
The steppe, same as ever.

393
00:22:14,710 --> 00:22:16,670
But is it really?

394
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:19,550
[TÖREGENE]
Good day to you, Great Khatun.

395
00:22:19,930 --> 00:22:22,060
Fine weather we're having.

396
00:22:22,600 --> 00:22:24,100
[SITARA]
It's as though it embodies

397
00:22:24,180 --> 00:22:26,680
the growing prosperity
of the empire.

398
00:22:28,020 --> 00:22:30,440
Yes, I would agree.

399
00:22:31,190 --> 00:22:33,570
Second Empress Töregene,

400
00:22:34,940 --> 00:22:36,650
and her lady-in-waiting,

401
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:38,740
Fatima.

402
00:22:39,780 --> 00:22:41,160
[Sitara chuckles]

403
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:42,620
♪

404
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:48,790
[SITARA (ADULT)] That year,
Emperor Ögedei

405
00:22:48,870 --> 00:22:51,500
appointed a governor
to oversee Persia.

406
00:22:52,340 --> 00:22:55,300
And the land that Sitara
once called home

407
00:22:55,380 --> 00:22:57,670
finally fell under
the permanent rule

408
00:22:57,760 --> 00:22:59,630
of the Mongol Empire.

409
00:23:00,340 --> 00:23:01,550
However...

410
00:23:01,970 --> 00:23:04,890
the dispute that this position
would cause...

411
00:23:04,970 --> 00:23:08,390
eventually, would turn into
a great storm

412
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:11,440
that would shake
the empire to its core.

413
00:23:12,150 --> 00:23:15,530
But no one knew this yet.

